          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guīdìng is built from guī 'a pair of compasses, a rule' and dìng 'to settle', both inherited from Middle Chinese, kjwie and dengH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'round' and the second 'calm'."
            }
